# The QA corpus is stored byte for byte.
#
# Several fixtures exist precisely to carry line terminators that are NOT the
# repository's convention: one file entirely in CRLF, one mixing CRLF and LF
# line by line, one with no terminator on its last line. Git's end-of-line
# conversion would rewrite exactly those bytes on checkout and on commit, and
# the requirement they verify — that every line keeps its own terminator — would
# be checked against fixtures that no longer contain the case.
#
# -text disables all conversion. Nothing here may relax it.
tests/qa/corpus/** -text
